[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186092314 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" "question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" "question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092315 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092316 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" "question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/id #uuid "b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143628" :question/problem "Mike has a total of $100$ candies divided into three bags. The first bag contains $18$ mint-flavored candies, while the second bag contains $16$ mint-flavored candies. If $55%$ of all of Mike's candies are mint-flavored, what is the probability that a randomly selected candy is a mint-flavored candy from the third bag?" :question/worked-solution "Let $M$ be the event that the selected candy is mint-flavored, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the selected candy is from the first bag,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the selected candy is from the second bag,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the selected candy is from the third bag.\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nRecall that the law of total probability states that\n\n$$\nP(M)=P(M\\cap A)+P(M\\cap B)+P(M\\cap C).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find $P(M\\cap C):$\n\n- To calculate $P(M\\cap A),$ we take the number of mint-flavored candies in the first bag $(18)$ and divide by the total number of candies $(100).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap A)=\\frac{18}{100}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(M\\cap B),$ we take the number of mint-flavored candies in the second bag $(16)$ and divide by the total number of candies$(100).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap B)=\\frac{16}{100}.\n$$\n\n- Also, we're given that\n\n$$\nP(M)=55%=\\frac{55}{100}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(M\\cap C),$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M) & =P(M\\cap A)+P(M\\cap B)+P(M\\cap C) \\\\ \\frac{55}{100} & =\\frac{18}{100}+\\frac{16}{100}+P(M\\cap C) \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =\\frac{55}{100}-\\frac{18}{100}-\\frac{16}{100} \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =\\frac{21}{100} \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =21%\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/id #uuid "b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer-field/choices ["answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" "answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" "answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" "answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" :answer/id #uuid "623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer/id #uuid "e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" :answer/id #uuid "1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" :answer/id #uuid "b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955" :answer/id #uuid "d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/id #uuid "c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/math-academy-id "q-143630" :question/problem "A certain disease is present in $500$ out of $100\\,000$ people in city $A,$ $800$ out of $200\\,000$ people in city $B,$ and $1\\,100$ out of $500\\,000$ people in city $C.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a person has the disease, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the person is from city $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the person is from city $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the person is from city $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person has the disease, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C)\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that there are a total of \n\n$$\n100\\,000+200\\,000+500\\,000=800\\,000\n$$\n\npeople in all three cities.\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap A),$ we take the number of people in city $A$ who have the disease $(500)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap A)=\\frac{500}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap B),$ we take the number of people in city $B$ who have the disease $(800)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap B)=\\frac{800}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap C),$ we take the number of people in city $C$ who have the disease $(1\\,100)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap C)=\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =\\frac{500}{800\\,000}+\\frac{800}{800\\,000}+\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\,400}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{8\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1\\,000}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" "answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" "answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" "answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" "answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer/id #uuid "b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{1\\,000}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" :answer/id #uuid "13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{1\\,100}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" :answer/id #uuid "70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{900}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" :answer/id #uuid "021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{1\\,500}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8" :answer/id #uuid "7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{800}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/id #uuid "4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/math-academy-id "q-143722" :question/problem "A total of $200$ colored table tennis balls are distributed among three boxes, $A,$ $B,$ and $C.$ Box $A$ contains $20$ green balls, while Box $B$ contains $30$ green balls. If $45%$ of all the balls are green, what is the probability that a randomly selected ball is a green ball from Box $C?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event that the selected ball is green, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $A$,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $B$,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nRecall that the law of total probability states that\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find $P(G\\cap C):$\n\n- To calculate $P(G\\cap A),$ we take the number of green balls in box $A$ $(20)$ and divide by the total number of balls $(200).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(G\\cap A)=\\frac{20}{200}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(G\\cap B),$ we take the number of green balls in box $B$ $(30)$ and divide by the total number of balls $(200).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(G\\cap B)=\\frac{30}{200}.\n$$\n\n- Also, we're given that\n\n$$\nP(G)=45%=\\frac{90}{200}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G\\cap C),$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\ \\frac{90}{200} & =\\frac{20}{200}+\\frac{30}{200}+P(G\\cap C) \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =\\frac{90}{200}-\\frac{20}{200}-\\frac{30}{200} \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =\\frac{40}{200} \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =20%\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" "answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" "answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" "answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" :answer/id #uuid "cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer/id #uuid "1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" :answer/id #uuid "94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" :answer/id #uuid "17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117" :answer/id #uuid "80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092558 :question/problem "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the components manufactured, $45%$ are produced by the first machine, $25%$ are produced by the second machine, and the third machine produces the remaining.\nIf $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, what is the probability that a randomly selected component is defective?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly selected component is defective, and \n\n- let ${B}_{1}$ be the event that the component was produced by the first machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{2}$ be the event that the component was produced by the second machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{3}$ be the event that the component was produced by the third machine.\n\nThen the disjoint union ${B}_{1}⊔{B}_{2}⊔{B}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap {B}_{1})+P(D\\cap {B}_{2})+P(D\\cap {B}_{3}) \\\\  & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the first machine produces $45%$ of the components, the second machine produces $25%$ of the components, the third machine produces the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(45%+25%)=30%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP({B}_{1})=0.45,\\,P({B}_{2})=0.25,\\,P({B}_{3})=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|{B}_{1})=0.08,\\,P(D|{B}_{2})=0.04,\\,P(D|{B}_{3})=0.05.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected component is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3}) \\\\  & =(0.08)(0.45)+(0.04)(0.25)+(0.05)(0.3) \\\\  & =0.036+0.01+0.015 \\\\  & =0.061.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186089519 :answer-field/correct 17592186089523 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/id #uuid "5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/math-academy-id "q-143752" :question/problem "In a particular park, there are three forests. Forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park area, and  $30%$ of its plants are poisonous. Forest $B$ occupies $25%$ of the park area, and $20%$ of its plants are poisonous. Forest $C$ occupies the remaining park area, and $6%$ of its plants are poisonous. What is the probability that a randomly selected plant from this park is poisonous? Assume that the plants are evenly distributed throughout the park." :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the event that the plant is poisonous, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the plant is from forest $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the plant is from forest $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the plant is from forest $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap A)+P(V\\cap B)+P(V\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park area and forest $B$ occupies $25%$, then forest $C$ occupies the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(40%+25%)=35%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.4,\\,P(B)=0.25,\\,P(C)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the plants in forest $A,$ $20%$ of the plants in forest $B$, and $6%$ of the plants in forrest $C$ are poisonous, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|A)=0.3,\\,P(V|B)=0.2,\\,P(V|C)=0.06.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected plant in that park is poisonous is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C) \\\\  & =(0.3)(0.4)+(0.2)(0.25)+(0.06)(0.35) \\\\  & =0.12+0.05+0.021 \\\\  & =0.191.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" "answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" "answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" "answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" :answer/id #uuid "09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.030" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" :answer/id #uuid "1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.035" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" :answer/id #uuid "83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.116" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer/id #uuid "89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.191" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258" :answer/id #uuid "ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.233" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/id #uuid "6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143945" :question/problem "In a particular national park, there are three forests. Forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park's total area, and $30%$ of the plants it contains are poisonous, while forest $B$ occupies $25%$ of the park's total area, and $20%$ of the plants it has are poisonous. Forest $C$ occupies the remaining area of the park. If the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ what percentage of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous? Assume that the plants are evenly distributed throughout the park." :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the event that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the plant is from forest $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the plant is from forest $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the plant is from forest $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap A)+P(V\\cap B)+P(V\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.  \n\n- Since forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the total park land and  forest $B$ occupies $25%$, then forest $C$ occupies the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(40%+25%)=35%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.4,\\,P(B)=0.25,\\,P(C)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the plants in forest $A$ and $20%$ of the plants in forest $B$ are poisonous, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|A)=0.3,\\,P(V|B)=0.2\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(V)=0.24.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(V|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C) \\\\ 0.24 & =(0.3)(0.4)+(0.2)(0.25)+P(V|C)(0.35) \\\\ 0.24 & =0.12+0.05+0.35P(V|C) \\\\ 0.35P(V|C) & =0.07 \\\\ P(V|C) & =0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" "answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" "answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" "answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" :answer/id #uuid "f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" :answer/id #uuid "745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer/id #uuid "53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" :answer/id #uuid "07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15" :answer/id #uuid "de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/id #uuid "6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/math-academy-id "q-143902" :question/problem "Three bags, $A,B,$ and $C,$ contain marbles. Bag $A$ contains $12$ red and $8$ green marbles, while bag $B$ contains $14$ red and $6$ green marbles. A bag is selected at random, and a marble is randomly selected from the bag. If the probability that the selected marble is green is $\\frac{2}{5},$  what proportion of marbles from bag $C$ are green?" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event of selecting a green marble at random from one of the three bags, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the marble is from bag $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the marble is from bag $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the marble is from bag $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a green marble, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $8$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $A,$ and  $6$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $B,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{8}{20},\\,P(G|B)=\\frac{6}{20}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability of picking a green marble  from one of the bags is $\\frac{2}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =(\\frac{8}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{6}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(G|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2}{15}+\\frac{1}{10}+(\\frac{1}{3})P(G|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{15}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the marbles from bag $C$ are green." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" "answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" "answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" "answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" "answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/id #uuid "3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/id #uuid "0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/id #uuid "49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/id #uuid "53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/id #uuid "fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/id #uuid "b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a"] ["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143628"] ["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/problem "Mike has a total of $100$ candies divided into three bags. The first bag contains $18$ mint-flavored candies, while the second bag contains $16$ mint-flavored candies. If $55%$ of all of Mike's candies are mint-flavored, what is the probability that a randomly selected candy is a mint-flavored candy from the third bag?"] ["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/worked-solution "Let $M$ be the event that the selected candy is mint-flavored, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the selected candy is from the first bag,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the selected candy is from the second bag,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the selected candy is from the third bag.\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nRecall that the law of total probability states that\n\n$$\nP(M)=P(M\\cap A)+P(M\\cap B)+P(M\\cap C).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find $P(M\\cap C):$\n\n- To calculate $P(M\\cap A),$ we take the number of mint-flavored candies in the first bag $(18)$ and divide by the total number of candies $(100).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap A)=\\frac{18}{100}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(M\\cap B),$ we take the number of mint-flavored candies in the second bag $(16)$ and divide by the total number of candies$(100).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap B)=\\frac{16}{100}.\n$$\n\n- Also, we're given that\n\n$$\nP(M)=55%=\\frac{55}{100}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(M\\cap C),$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M) & =P(M\\cap A)+P(M\\cap B)+P(M\\cap C) \\\\ \\frac{55}{100} & =\\frac{18}{100}+\\frac{16}{100}+P(M\\cap C) \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =\\frac{55}{100}-\\frac{18}{100}-\\frac{16}{100} \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =\\frac{21}{100} \\\\ P(M\\cap C) & =21%\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/id #uuid "b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06"] ["answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" :answer/id #uuid "623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d"] ["answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d" :answer/value "20%"] ["answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer/id #uuid "e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071"] ["answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071" :answer/value "21%"] ["answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" :answer/id #uuid "1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3"] ["answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3" :answer/value "22%"] ["answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" :answer/id #uuid "b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad"] ["answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad" :answer/value "23%"] ["answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955" :answer/id #uuid "d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955"] ["answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955" :answer/value "25%"] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/correct "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071"] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/choices "answer-623f5887-d90a-5fd9-995d-57c77b99a09d"] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/choices "answer-e9dd86a2-28a9-54a1-bd47-96969ce92071"] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/choices "answer-1eeceee9-6b7e-5700-a74d-8554e7f70cc3"] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/choices "answer-b545930d-e0e3-5eee-bcf2-24a05aca55ad"] ["answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06" :answer-field/choices "answer-d0fd87a2-4baf-59fc-a98d-12d7d2b4e955"] ["question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b160229e-63c8-5bb3-85c1-a2c73ec30a06"] [17592186092314 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b1ef773a-e0ea-5eef-bbf3-332e3e7efe2a"] ["question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/id #uuid "c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241"] ["question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/math-academy-id "q-143630"] ["question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/problem "A certain disease is present in $500$ out of $100\\,000$ people in city $A,$ $800$ out of $200\\,000$ people in city $B,$ and $1\\,100$ out of $500\\,000$ people in city $C.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease?"] ["question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a person has the disease, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the person is from city $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the person is from city $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the person is from city $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person has the disease, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C)\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that there are a total of \n\n$$\n100\\,000+200\\,000+500\\,000=800\\,000\n$$\n\npeople in all three cities.\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap A),$ we take the number of people in city $A$ who have the disease $(500)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap A)=\\frac{500}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap B),$ we take the number of people in city $B$ who have the disease $(800)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap B)=\\frac{800}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap C),$ we take the number of people in city $C$ who have the disease $(1\\,100)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap C)=\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =\\frac{500}{800\\,000}+\\frac{800}{800\\,000}+\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\,400}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{8\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1\\,000}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c"] ["answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer/id #uuid "b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266"] ["answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{1\\,000}"] ["answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" :answer/id #uuid "13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2"] ["answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{1\\,100}"] ["answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" :answer/id #uuid "70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f"] ["answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{900}"] ["answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" :answer/id #uuid "021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37"] ["answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{1\\,500}"] ["answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8" :answer/id #uuid "7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8"] ["answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8" :answer/value "\\frac{9}{800}"] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/correct "answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266"] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/choices "answer-b33a5833-4704-5b74-8d07-51d290832266"] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/choices "answer-13f621be-7da4-57ec-be1a-3bb71fd27cb2"] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/choices "answer-70fa78ce-a5bb-554d-89bf-e9ff2f2c268f"] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/choices "answer-021e9a8f-b7c8-5617-b841-181c6dabad37"] ["answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c" :answer-field/choices "answer-7c0bd94e-0737-59fd-971d-a9571075b9e8"] ["question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1ddb04e3-1a47-50bb-8bb5-20ad79469f4c"] [17592186092314 :knowledge-point/questions "question-c3e46311-f49f-5429-9145-049194bfe241"] ["question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/id #uuid "4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89"] ["question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/math-academy-id "q-143722"] ["question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/problem "A total of $200$ colored table tennis balls are distributed among three boxes, $A,$ $B,$ and $C.$ Box $A$ contains $20$ green balls, while Box $B$ contains $30$ green balls. If $45%$ of all the balls are green, what is the probability that a randomly selected ball is a green ball from Box $C?$"] ["question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event that the selected ball is green, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $A$,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $B$,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the selected ball is from box $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nRecall that the law of total probability states that\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find $P(G\\cap C):$\n\n- To calculate $P(G\\cap A),$ we take the number of green balls in box $A$ $(20)$ and divide by the total number of balls $(200).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(G\\cap A)=\\frac{20}{200}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(G\\cap B),$ we take the number of green balls in box $B$ $(30)$ and divide by the total number of balls $(200).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(G\\cap B)=\\frac{30}{200}.\n$$\n\n- Also, we're given that\n\n$$\nP(G)=45%=\\frac{90}{200}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G\\cap C),$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\ \\frac{90}{200} & =\\frac{20}{200}+\\frac{30}{200}+P(G\\cap C) \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =\\frac{90}{200}-\\frac{20}{200}-\\frac{30}{200} \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =\\frac{40}{200} \\\\ P(G\\cap C) & =20%\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b"] ["answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" :answer/id #uuid "cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac"] ["answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac" :answer/value "15%"] ["answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer/id #uuid "1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6"] ["answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6" :answer/value "20%"] ["answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" :answer/id #uuid "94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546"] ["answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546" :answer/value "25%"] ["answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" :answer/id #uuid "17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6"] ["answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6" :answer/value "30%"] ["answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117" :answer/id #uuid "80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117"] ["answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117" :answer/value "35%"] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/correct "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6"] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/choices "answer-cd730609-69cd-5dce-ba00-d82c5d65d5ac"] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/choices "answer-1a9d603e-b926-5237-8790-115938fc5ec6"] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/choices "answer-94008e65-8008-5f2f-98cd-a9a293d66546"] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/choices "answer-17b422f9-8fe0-59bc-9eec-efa1f37dfae6"] ["answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b" :answer-field/choices "answer-80f55f6c-60e9-5aa3-80c4-2b3c42adb117"] ["question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9aa2967b-23f5-554f-85ed-580439a3657b"] [17592186092314 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4c96dcfa-0dd7-50ec-b775-86d1b3c50f89"] [17592186092558 :question/problem "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the components manufactured, $45%$ are produced by the first machine, $25%$ are produced by the second machine, and the third machine produces the remaining.\nIf $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, what is the probability that a randomly selected component is defective?"] [17592186092558 :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly selected component is defective, and \n\n- let ${B}_{1}$ be the event that the component was produced by the first machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{2}$ be the event that the component was produced by the second machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{3}$ be the event that the component was produced by the third machine.\n\nThen the disjoint union ${B}_{1}⊔{B}_{2}⊔{B}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap {B}_{1})+P(D\\cap {B}_{2})+P(D\\cap {B}_{3}) \\\\  & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the first machine produces $45%$ of the components, the second machine produces $25%$ of the components, the third machine produces the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(45%+25%)=30%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP({B}_{1})=0.45,\\,P({B}_{2})=0.25,\\,P({B}_{3})=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|{B}_{1})=0.08,\\,P(D|{B}_{2})=0.04,\\,P(D|{B}_{3})=0.05.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected component is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3}) \\\\  & =(0.08)(0.45)+(0.04)(0.25)+(0.05)(0.3) \\\\  & =0.036+0.01+0.015 \\\\  & =0.061.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186092558 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186089519 :answer-field/correct 17592186089523] ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/id #uuid "5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03"] ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/math-academy-id "q-143752"] ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/problem "In a particular park, there are three forests. Forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park area, and  $30%$ of its plants are poisonous. Forest $B$ occupies $25%$ of the park area, and $20%$ of its plants are poisonous. Forest $C$ occupies the remaining park area, and $6%$ of its plants are poisonous. What is the probability that a randomly selected plant from this park is poisonous? Assume that the plants are evenly distributed throughout the park."] ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the event that the plant is poisonous, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the plant is from forest $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the plant is from forest $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the plant is from forest $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap A)+P(V\\cap B)+P(V\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park area and forest $B$ occupies $25%$, then forest $C$ occupies the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(40%+25%)=35%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.4,\\,P(B)=0.25,\\,P(C)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the plants in forest $A,$ $20%$ of the plants in forest $B$, and $6%$ of the plants in forrest $C$ are poisonous, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|A)=0.3,\\,P(V|B)=0.2,\\,P(V|C)=0.06.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected plant in that park is poisonous is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C) \\\\  & =(0.3)(0.4)+(0.2)(0.25)+(0.06)(0.35) \\\\  & =0.12+0.05+0.021 \\\\  & =0.191.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b"] ["answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" :answer/id #uuid "09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6"] ["answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6" :answer/value "0.030"] ["answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" :answer/id #uuid "1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e"] ["answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e" :answer/value "0.035"] ["answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" :answer/id #uuid "83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2"] ["answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2" :answer/value "0.116"] ["answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer/id #uuid "89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569"] ["answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569" :answer/value "0.191"] ["answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258" :answer/id #uuid "ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258"] ["answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258" :answer/value "0.233"] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/correct "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569"] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/choices "answer-09666b40-5355-57b1-8b42-60c63995a1c6"] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/choices "answer-1f8ba24e-a713-55d8-8ec1-c3ba12f16e7e"] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/choices "answer-83b5f13c-3fd2-5d10-b864-2eb89194f1c2"] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/choices "answer-89585630-1207-54f3-a6dd-d0dda6b0d569"] ["answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b" :answer-field/choices "answer-ce33935e-f5d0-55b5-9281-89fcc88c0258"] ["question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ed1fa99e-a491-5eba-bafa-dde6be00551b"] [17592186092315 :knowledge-point/questions "question-5295db33-6fb5-59ca-9a76-f6dda26f7e03"] ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/id #uuid "6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c"] ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143945"] ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/problem "In a particular national park, there are three forests. Forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park's total area, and $30%$ of the plants it contains are poisonous, while forest $B$ occupies $25%$ of the park's total area, and $20%$ of the plants it has are poisonous. Forest $C$ occupies the remaining area of the park. If the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ what percentage of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous? Assume that the plants are evenly distributed throughout the park."] ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the event that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the plant is from forest $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the plant is from forest $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the plant is from forest $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap A)+P(V\\cap B)+P(V\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.  \n\n- Since forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the total park land and  forest $B$ occupies $25%$, then forest $C$ occupies the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(40%+25%)=35%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.4,\\,P(B)=0.25,\\,P(C)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the plants in forest $A$ and $20%$ of the plants in forest $B$ are poisonous, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|A)=0.3,\\,P(V|B)=0.2\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(V)=0.24.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(V|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C) \\\\ 0.24 & =(0.3)(0.4)+(0.2)(0.25)+P(V|C)(0.35) \\\\ 0.24 & =0.12+0.05+0.35P(V|C) \\\\ 0.35P(V|C) & =0.07 \\\\ P(V|C) & =0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous."] ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5"] ["answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" :answer/id #uuid "f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60"] ["answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60" :answer/value "12%"] ["answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" :answer/id #uuid "745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db"] ["answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db" :answer/value "18%"] ["answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer/id #uuid "53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1"] ["answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1" :answer/value "20%"] ["answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" :answer/id #uuid "07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04"] ["answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04" :answer/value "22%"] ["answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15" :answer/id #uuid "de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15"] ["answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15" :answer/value "25%"] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/correct "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1"] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/choices "answer-f673d168-be18-50e2-a30f-7e13848f8d60"] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/choices "answer-745015e3-e981-5fcb-a0d8-9fc8adee58db"] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/choices "answer-53550687-5bc6-5d71-b56f-d4df929d00c1"] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/choices "answer-07a8bb0b-fd79-5284-a3d7-a5bcb76e5c04"] ["answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5" :answer-field/choices "answer-de4f9499-4120-5b2b-9957-fb77ce79db15"] ["question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-81cebeb7-8aa0-5776-9a06-8fc04eda14d5"] [17592186092316 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6f97d30d-8f92-59ad-aa37-53ebf51b3b4c"] ["question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/id #uuid "6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d"] ["question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/math-academy-id "q-143902"] ["question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/problem "Three bags, $A,B,$ and $C,$ contain marbles. Bag $A$ contains $12$ red and $8$ green marbles, while bag $B$ contains $14$ red and $6$ green marbles. A bag is selected at random, and a marble is randomly selected from the bag. If the probability that the selected marble is green is $\\frac{2}{5},$  what proportion of marbles from bag $C$ are green?"] ["question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event of selecting a green marble at random from one of the three bags, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the marble is from bag $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the marble is from bag $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the marble is from bag $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a green marble, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $8$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $A,$ and  $6$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $B,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{8}{20},\\,P(G|B)=\\frac{6}{20}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability of picking a green marble  from one of the bags is $\\frac{2}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =(\\frac{8}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{6}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(G|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2}{15}+\\frac{1}{10}+(\\frac{1}{3})P(G|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{15}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the marbles from bag $C$ are green."] ["question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111"] ["answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/id #uuid "3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7"] ["answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/id #uuid "0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca"] ["answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/id #uuid "49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde"] ["answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/id #uuid "53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d"] ["answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/id #uuid "fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6"] ["answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}"] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/correct "answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7"] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/choices "answer-3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7"] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/choices "answer-0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca"] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/choices "answer-49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde"] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/choices "answer-53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d"] ["answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/choices "answer-fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6"] ["question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111"] [17592186092316 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d"]] "retractions" [[17592186092558 :question/problem "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the components manufactured, $45%$ are produced by the first machine, $25%$ are produced by the second machine, and the third machine produces the remaining.\nIf $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, what is the probability that a randomly selected component is defective?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."]]}]